   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "1. The nine planets who were worshipped in many ways with devotion for a ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    137,
    556,
    152
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "long time by sage Parasara, having been pleased bestowed upon him the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    161,
    556,
    176
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "knowledge of accurately determining their effects (on births in this world). Being ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    185,
    556,
    201
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "convinced after many tests that they are unfailing, I take out the essence from the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    209,
    556,
    225
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "astrological scripts containing his famous sayings and set forth the famous Maha ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    233,
    556,
    249
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Dasa.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    257,
    117,
    273
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "2. Count the stars from Krittika in groups of nine. The planets presiding over ",
   "bbox": [
    121,
    282,
    556,
    297
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "the dasas belonging to the nine nakshatras composing each group are respectively ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    306,
    556,
    321
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "the Sun, the Moon, Mars, Rahu, Jupiter, Saturn, Mercury, Ketu and Venus and the ",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    330,
    556,
    345
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "span of their dasa periods are respectively 6, 10, 7, 18, 16, 19, 17, 7 and 20 year.",
   "bbox": [
    85,
    354,
    535,
    370
   ]
  },
